# The pinned matrix for Run-Raft. Both runners read this file, so the set of configurations and the outcome
# each must produce are stated once rather than in two places that can drift apart.
#
# Each row is the configuration, the specification, the expected outcome, and for a negative the invariant it
# must break, separated by tabs. Blank lines and lines opening with a hash are ignored. The modules SANY
# parses are the distinct specifications named here, in the order they first appear, so a specification
# reaches SANY by having a configuration rather than by being listed a second time.
#
# An expected red run is a negative model: a configuration that enables a forbidden behaviour or removes a
# shipped guard, and whose run must report a violation. A green negative means the model lost its defect and
# its positive runs prove nothing. A red run must also break the invariant named here, because a negative
# that goes red on something else has stopped testing what it was written for.
#
# Each log pair is a negative and the positive it licenses, at identical constants. The bound a pair runs at
# is the one its own negative goes red at, so it cannot be shortened without making the pair meaningless. All
# four quotient the state space by ServerSymmetry, which is what holds MCRaftLogFigure8 to about ninety
# seconds instead of the forty minutes the brute-force run over the same bound costs.
MCRaftElectionClosed.cfg	RaftElection.tla	green
MCRaftElectionOutsiderUnguarded.cfg	RaftElection.tla	red	ElectionSafety
MCRaftElectionOutsiderGuarded.cfg	RaftElection.tla	green
MCRaftElectionTermInflation.cfg	RaftElection.tla	red	NoTermInflation
MCRaftElectionFilterFirst.cfg	RaftElection.tla	green
MCRaftLogVolatileReplicas.cfg	RaftLog.tla	red	CommittedIsDurableAtAQuorum
MCRaftLogDurable.cfg	RaftLog.tla	green
MCRaftLogFigure8Withdrawn.cfg	RaftLog.tla	red	LeaderCompleteness
MCRaftLogFigure8.cfg	RaftLog.tla	green
